   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Code Smell Detection using Weave and LiteLLM\n",
    "\n",
    "Detecting code smells—patterns indicating design problems—is crucial for maintaining software quality. This guide demonstrates an end-to-end pipeline for identifying and evaluating code smells in a Java codebase.\n",
    "\n",
    "We'll use Weave for tracking, versioning, and evaluating our pipeline, and `litellm` to interact with language models for analysis and evaluation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Why use Weave?\n",
    "\n",
    "In this tutorial, we'll use Weave to implement and evaluate our code smell detection pipeline. You'll learn how to:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Track your LLM pipeline**: Log inputs, outputs, and intermediate steps of the analysis and evaluation process.\n",
    "2. **Evaluate LLM outputs**: Create and compare evaluations of the detected code smells against a ground truth dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Set up the environment\n",
    "\n",
    "First, let's set up our environment and import the necessary libraries:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%pip install -q -U wandb weave litellm \"langchain-google-genai\" \"deeplake<4.0.0\" \"langchain\" \"langchain-text-splitters\" \"langchain-community\" \"tiktoken\" \"google-ai-generativelanguage==0.6.15\" python-dotenv python-frontmatter"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import weave\n",
    "import litellm\n",
    "from glob import glob\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import enum\n",
    "import json\n",
    "from IPython.display import Markdown, display\n",
    "from langchain.output_parsers import PydanticOutputParser\n",
    "from langchain.vectorstores import DeepLake\n",
    "from langchain.document_loaders import TextLoader\n",
    "from langchain_text_splitters import MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter\n",
    "from langchain_google_genai import GoogleGenerativeAIEmbeddings\n",
    "from langchain.schema import Document\n",
    "from pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n",
    "from typing import List, Optional, Dict\n",
    "from weave import Dataset, Evaluation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "os.environ['WANDB_API_KEY'] = '36b71dbd9487c532ea14d42d0e639a55e3081ef0'\n",
    "# Replace with your Google API key or load from a .env file\n",
    "# from dotenv import load_dotenv\n",
    "# load_dotenv()\n",
    "# os.environ[\"GOOGLE_API_KEY\"] = os.getenv(\"GOOGLE_API_KEY\")\n",
    "\n",
    "WEAVE_PROJECT = \"smellai-litellm-restructured\"\n",
    "weave.init(WEAVE_PROJECT)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Building the Knowledge Base\n",
    "\n",
    "We create a RAG pipeline to provide the LLM with context about code smells. The knowledge base is built from a repository of code smell definitions and stored in a DeepLake vector store."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!git clone https://github.com/watabou/pixel-dungeon.git\n",
    "!git clone https://github.com/Luzkan/smells.git"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "smells_match = \"smells/content/smells/**/*.md\"\n",
    "all_smells = glob(smells_match, recursive=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "headers_to_split_on = [(\"#\", \"Title\"), (\"##\", \"Section\"), (\"###\", \"Subsection\")]\n",
    "docs = []\n",
    "for file in all_smells:\n",
    "    with open(file, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
    "        content = f.read()\n",
    "    if '---' in content:\n",
    "        parts = content.split('---', 2)\n",
    "        markdown_content = '--' + parts[2] if len(parts) >= 3 else content\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        markdown_content = content\n",
    "    markdown_splitter = MarkdownHeaderTextSplitter(headers_to_split_on=headers_to_split_on)\n",
    "    header_splits = markdown_splitter.split_text(markdown_content)\n",
    "    for doc in header_splits:\n",
    "        doc.metadata['source'] = file\n",
    "    docs.extend(header_splits)\n",
    "\n",
    "embeddings = GoogleGenerativeAIEmbeddings(model=\"models/text-embedding-004\")\n",
    "dataset_path = 'mem://deeplake/smells'\n",
    "smell_db = DeepLake.from_documents(docs, embeddings, dataset_path=dataset_path)\n",
    "retriever = smell_db.as_retriever()\n",
    "retriever.search_kwargs['distance_metric'] = 'cos'\n",
    "retriever.search_kwargs['k'] = 20"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Leveraging Structured Outputs and Pydantic Models\n",
    "\n",
    "We use Pydantic models to define the expected structure of the LLM's output. This ensures type safety, easier parsing, and improved reliability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class CodeSmellSeverity(str, enum.Enum):\n",
    "    HIGH = \"HIGH\"\n",
    "    MEDIUM = \"MEDIUM\"\n",
    "    LOW = \"LOW\"\n",
    "\n",
    "class CodeSmellDetection(BaseModel):\n",
    "    smell_type: str = Field(description=\"The type of code smell detected\")\n",
    "    location: str = Field(description=\"Where in the code the smell was found\")\n",
    "    severity: CodeSmellSeverity = Field(description=\"How severe the smell is\")\n",
    "    description: str = Field(description=\"Brief explanation of the issue\")\n",
    "    refactoring_suggestion: str = Field(description=\"How to fix the code smell\")\n",
    "\n",
    "class CodeAnalysisResult(BaseModel):\n",
    "    analysis_summary: str = Field(description=\"Overall summary of code quality\")\n",
    "    smells_detected: List[CodeSmellDetection] = Field(description=\"List of detected code smells\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Define the Code Analysis Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "We encapsulate our analysis logic in a `CodeAnalysisModel`, a `weave.Model` subclass. This automatically versions the model and tracks its parameters, like `llm_model` and `temperature`. The `predict` method, decorated with `@weave.op()`, logs all inputs and outputs to Weave."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class CodeAnalysisModel(weave.Model):\n",
    "    llm_model: str\n",
    "    temperature: float\n",
    "\n",
    "    @weave.op()\n",
    "    def predict(self, file_path: str) -> Optional[CodeAnalysisResult]:\n",
    "        with open(file_path, 'r') as f:\n",
    "            code_content = f.read()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        CodeSmell = enum.Enum('CodeSmell', {p.stem.replace('-', '_').upper(): p.stem for p in Path('smells/content/smells').rglob('*.md')})\n",
    "        valid_smells = [smell.name for smell in CodeSmell]\n",
    "        \n",
    "        parser = PydanticOutputParser(pydantic_object=CodeAnalysisResult)\n",
    "        retrieved_docs = retriever.get_relevant_documents(code_content)\n",
    "        retrieved_context = "\n".join([doc.page_content for doc in retrieved_docs])\n",
    "        \n",
    "        prompt = f"""\n",
    "        You are an expert code analyst. Analyze the following code for code smells based on the provided context.\n",
    "        **Context on Code Smells:**\n{retrieved_context}\n\n",
    "        **Code to Analyze:**\n```java\n{code_content}```\n\n",
    "        **Instructions:**\nOnly identify code smells from this list: {valid_smells}.\n",
    "        Format your response as a structured JSON object matching this schema:\n{format_instructions}\n"""
",
    "        \n",
    "        formatted_prompt = prompt.format(\n",
    "            retrieved_context=retrieved_context,\n",
    "            code_content=code_content,\n",
    "            valid_smells=valid_smells,\n",
    "            format_instructions=parser.get_format_instructions()\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            response = litellm.completion(\n",
    "                model=self.llm_model,\n",
    "                messages=[{"role": "user", "content": formatted_prompt}],\n",
    "                temperature=self.temperature,\n",
    "                response_format={ \"type\": \"json_object\" }\n",
    "            )\n",
    "            response_content = response.choices[0].message.content\n",
    "            if isinstance(response_content, str):\n",
    "                response_json = json.loads(response_content)\n",
    "            else:\n",
    "                response_json = response_content\n",
    "            return CodeAnalysisResult.parse_obj(response_json)\n",
    "        except Exception as e:\n",
    "            print(f"Error during code analysis: {e}")\n",
    "            return None"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Implement evaluation metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "To assess the quality of our analysis, we define evaluation metrics and an evaluation model. The `score` function will be used by Weave's `Evaluation` to compare the model's output against the ground truth."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class EvaluationScore(str, enum.Enum):\n",
    "    EXCELLENT = \"EXCELLENT\"\n",
    "    GOOD = \"GOOD\"\n",
    "    ACCEPTABLE = \"ACCEPTABLE\"\n",
    "    POOR = \"POOR\"\n",
    "    INCORRECT = \"INCORRECT\"\n",
    "\n",
    "class SmellEvaluation(BaseModel):\n",
    "    detected_smell: str\n",
    "    score: EvaluationScore\n",
    "    justification: str\n",
    "\n",
    "class CodeSmellEvaluationResult(BaseModel):\n",
    "    overall_score: float\n",
    "    precision: float\n",
    "    recall: float\n",
    "    evaluations: List[SmellEvaluation]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "@weave.op()\n",
    "def score(ground_truth: Dict, model_output: Optional[CodeAnalysisResult]) -> Dict:\n",
    "    if model_output is None:\n",
    "        return {\"correct\": False, \"error\": \"Model failed to produce output\"}\n",
    "    \n",
    "    detected_smells = model_output.smells_detected\n",
    "    ground_truth_smells = ground_truth['smells']\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # This is a simplified scoring logic. A more robust implementation would\n",
    "    # involve more sophisticated matching of locations and smell types.\n",
    "    correctly_identified = 0\n",
    "    for detected in detected_smells:\n",
    "        for truth in ground_truth_smells:\n",
    "            if detected.smell_type.lower() in truth['smell_type'].lower():\n",
    "                correctly_identified += 1\n",
    "                break\n",
    "    \n",
    "    precision = correctly_identified / len(detected_smells) if detected_smells else 0\n",
    "    recall = correctly_identified / len(ground_truth_smells) if ground_truth_smells else 0\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return {\"precision\": precision, \"recall\": recall}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Create a Weave Dataset and run evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "To evaluate our pipeline, we'll create a Weave Dataset from our ground truth data and then run an `Evaluation`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "evaluation_files = {\n",
    "    \"pixel-dungeon/src/com/watabou/pixeldungeon/levels/HallsLevel.java\": {\n",
    "        \"smells\": [\n",
    "            {\"smell_type\": \"MAGIC_NUMBER\", \"location\": \"multiple locations\"},\n",
    "            {\"smell_type\": \"LONG_METHOD\", \"location\": \"decorate() method\"}\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "dataset_rows = []\n",
    "for file_path, ground_truth in evaluation_files.items():\n",
    "    dataset_rows.append({
     "file_path": file_path, 
     "ground_truth": ground_truth
    })\n",
    "\n",
    "smell_dataset = Dataset(name=\"code-smell-evaluation-dataset\", rows=dataset_rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "weave.publish(smell_dataset)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "analysis_model = CodeAnalysisModel(llm_model=\"gemini/gemini-pro\", temperature=0.2)\n",
    "\n",
    "evaluation = Evaluation(\n",
    "    name=\"code-smell-detection-evaluation\",\n",
    "    dataset=smell_dataset,\n",
    "    scorers=[score]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# This will run the model on each example in the dataset and call the scorer\n",
    "# The results will be visible in the Weave UI\n",
    "evaluation.evaluate(analysis_model)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "In this example, we've demonstrated how to implement a code smell detection pipeline using Weave and LiteLLM. We've shown how to:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Create Weave operations for each step of the analysis process.\n",
    "2. Wrap the pipeline in a Weave Model for easy tracking and evaluation.\n",
    "3. Implement custom evaluation metrics using Weave operations.\n",
    "4. Create a Weave Dataset and run an evaluation of the pipeline.\n",
    "\n",
    "Weave's seamless integration allows us to track inputs, outputs, and intermediate steps throughout the code smell detection process, making it easier to debug, optimize, and evaluate our LLM application."
   ]
  }
